      "text": "To find the smallest positive value of $x$ such that $x + 5678$ is a palindrome, we can reverse engineer that concept.\n\nA palindrome always remains the same when reversed. This means if we negate $x$ in the given equation, combining that $-x$ with $5678$ + $x$ will result in the same final output. To compose a palindrome using a given input (5678 in our case), $x$ must factorize the factorial of 5678's inverse. This is the best use of that given input.\n\nSo, we must calculate the factorial of 5678's inverse to find the answer. This presents the maximum possible number that can be formed in every direction given the basic requirement that the result must be a palindrome and greater than $x$ itself.\n\nHence, the final answer is the factorial of the integer part of 5678 squared minus 1.",
